// t_36492ad8 commit 2.  Measured against sce-cgc 475.
// OVERLOAD RANKING PUTS NARROWING LAST, and this is the shape that proved it.
// `clamp(f, 0, 1)` with a float f appears verbatim in five SDK shaders
// (MachoQHDR x4 and stereo3D/fp_anaglyph).  Two candidates are viable:
// clamp(float,float,float) needs two WIDENINGS, clamp(int,int,int) needs one
// NARROWING.  Under a single additive cost with "a demotion costs twice a
// promotion" those come to the same number, the call ties, and a tie is
// C1101 - which refused all five shaders that both the reference and our own
// parent compiled.  Counting narrowings separately and comparing them FIRST
// is what the reference does.
float4 main(float4 t : TEXCOORD0) : COLOR { float f = t.x; return clamp(f, 0, 1); }
